From c94f9ff481a8bd782382530b9b21e4a00e836ee3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick <nekreshen@yandex.ru>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:08:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] metal: volume textures, depth bias, resolves into mip
 levels, GPU fences only after resolves, MetalFX present upscale, stall
 reports

- Volume (3D) textures load, tiled (Xenos 3D tiling) or linear, into
  MTLTextureType3D. FIFA 19's tone map grades colour through two 32x32x32
  LUTs; sampled as zero they left every match black.
- Polygon offset (PA_SU_POLY_OFFSET_*) applied as the Vulkan backend does.
- metal_resolve_into_mips: a resolve that lands exactly on a level of a loaded
  tiled texture with mips is blitted into that level and the texture kept.
  FIFA's 2048x2048 k_4_4_4_4 downsample chain reloaded 8 MB+ per level.
- metal_gpu_fences: a fence with no resolve since the last one (and no GPU
  fence still pending) is written at once; metal_gpu_fences_all writes every
  one on the GPU. Stats count both.
- metal_present_upscale=metalfx: MetalFX spatial upscaling of the guest output
  to the window (SDR only).
- metal_hitch_log_ms (250): a log line per slow frame; metal_stall_sample_ms
  (off): /usr/bin/sample of every thread when no swap came for that long.
